{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/kuni9w","slideIndex":8,"text":"This prototype is deliberately honest about its limits. The models are enlarged educational illustrations, not scans or clinically validated anatomy. They do not simulate flow, pressure, contraction, or continuous morphing. Next, I would seek expert review, test comfort and usability, then measure comprehension and retention with medical students. The goal is evidence that spatial interaction helps learners understand and remember the sequence."}